{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Logic.Relation","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.TypeTags.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Equiv.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":62,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheScaled_normalise_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheScaled_normalise_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":524,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L524-L533","doc":"**The normalised witness above is the constant function `1`** — stated so that the limit of what\n`writheScaled_normalise_isMarkovInvariant` witnesses is machine-checked rather than left to prose.\n`c^{writhe} · d^{level}` at `c = A⁻¹, d = D⁻¹` is the exact inverse of `writheScaled A D`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheScaled_normalise_isMarkovInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheScaled_normalise_isMarkovInvariant","kind":"theorem","line":507,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L507-L522","doc":"The normalised writhe functional is therefore a Markov invariant — the full chain\n(`IsScaledMarkov` ⇒ normalise ⇒ `IsMarkovInvariant` ⇒ descent) instantiated end to end.\n\n**Read with `writheScaled_normalise_eq_one`, which is the honest scope of this instance.** On this\ntower the normalisation cancels the functional exactly, so the resulting invariant is the *constant*\n`1`. That is the correct mathematics — the abelianised tower retains only the writhe, which is\nprecisely what the framing correction removes — but it means this theorem witnesses only that the\nhypothesis set of `normalise_isMarkovInvariant` is non-empty, **not** that a non-trivial normalised\ninvariant has been produced. Non-constant satisfiability of `IsMarkovInvariant` is carried by\n`writheParity_isMarkovInvariant`, and non-triviality of `MarkovEquiv` by\n`writheTower_not_markovEquiv`; neither is a corollary of this one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheScaled_normalisation_solvable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheScaled_normalisation_solvable","kind":"theorem","line":498,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L498-L505","doc":"The two normalisation equations `c * d * a = 1` and `d * b = c` are **solvable** for this\nfamily: `c = A⁻¹`, `d = D⁻¹`. So `IsScaledMarkov.normalise_isMarkovInvariant` has a non-empty\nhypothesis set, and its conclusion is reachable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheScaled_isScaledMarkov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheScaled_isScaledMarkov","kind":"theorem","line":476,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L476-L496","doc":"`writheScaled` satisfies the `IsScaledMarkov` axioms with `a = A * D` and `b = A⁻¹ * D`, so the\nscaled interface is satisfiable with non-trivial parameters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheScaled_mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheScaled_mk","kind":"theorem","line":473,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L473-L474","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheScaled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheScaled","kind":"def","line":467,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L467-L471","doc":"A scaled Markov functional on the writhe tower with values in a commutative ring: `A` to the\nwrithe times `D` to the level. Its Markov parameters are `A * D` and `A⁻¹ * D`, both non-trivial in\ngeneral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheTower_not_markovEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheTower_not_markovEquiv","kind":"theorem","line":452,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L452-L463","doc":"**`MarkovEquiv` is a proper relation** — not everything is equivalent to everything. The two\nelements of writhe `0` and writhe `1` at level `0` have different writhe parity, so no sequence of\nMarkov moves connects them. Together with `writheTower_markovEquiv_cross_level` this places the\nrelation strictly between equality and the total relation, so neither it nor\n`IsMarkovInvariant.descends` is vacuous. (Both sides are elements of `Multiplicative ℤ`; no\ntopological reading of them is intended or available here.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.not_markovEquiv_of_writheParity_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.not_markovEquiv_of_writheParity_ne","kind":"theorem","line":446,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L446-L450","doc":"Two elements with different writhe-parity are **not** Markov equivalent. Contrapositive of the\ndescent theorem, and the reason `writheParity` was worth building. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheParity_isMarkovInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheParity_isMarkovInvariant","kind":"theorem","line":425,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L425-L444","doc":"`writheParity` satisfies all three invariance conditions — so `IsMarkovInvariant` is satisfiable\nby something that is not constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheParity_mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheParity_mk","kind":"theorem","line":422,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L422-L423","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheParity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheParity","kind":"def","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L410-L420","doc":"**A genuine Markov invariant on the writhe tower**: writhe plus level, read mod 2. Positive\nstabilisation raises both by one (sum unchanged mod 2); negative stabilisation lowers the writhe and\nraises the level (sum unchanged mod 2); move I is invisible because the group is abelian.\n\n**Not a new result — it is used here only as a non-vacuity witness.** The corpus already carries\nthis parity on a concrete `(writhe, level)` pair model, and carries it further than this file does:\n`QOU.StandardModel.LevelParity.markovPair_parity` proves the same invariance and\n`markovPair_of_even` proves the parity is *complete* for that model (any two pairs of equal parity\nare Markov-related). No completeness claim is made here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheTower_markovEquiv_cross_level","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheTower_markovEquiv_cross_level","kind":"theorem","line":401,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L401-L408","doc":"The two Markov moves genuinely relate **different levels**: the trivial braid on `n` strands is\nMarkov equivalent to a one-crossing braid on `n+1` strands. So `MarkovEquiv` is strictly coarser than\nequality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheFraming","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheFraming","kind":"def","line":395,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L395-L399","doc":"The tautological framing of the writhe tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheTower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.writheTower","kind":"def","line":389,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L389-L393","doc":"The abelianised (writhe) tower: every level is `Multiplicative ℤ`, stabilisation is the\nidentity, and the new generator has writhe one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsScaledMarkov.normalise_descends","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsScaledMarkov.normalise_descends","kind":"theorem","line":374,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L374-L380","doc":"**Descent for a scaled Markov functional**, in one step: Markov-equivalent braids have equal\n*normalised* values. This is the statement a Jones-type invariant actually needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsScaledMarkov.normalise_isMarkovInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsScaledMarkov.normalise_isMarkovInvariant","kind":"theorem","line":337,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L337-L372","doc":"**The Jones normalisation, abstractly.** If `f` is a scaled Markov functional with parameters\n`a, b`, and the scalars `c, d` solve the two equations\n\n    c * d * a = 1        (positive stabilisation is cancelled)\n    d * b = c            (negative stabilisation is cancelled)\n\nthen `c^{writhe} · d^{level} · f` is a genuine Markov invariant, hence descends to Markov classes by\n`IsMarkovInvariant.descends`.\n\nThe two equations are not decoration: eliminating `d` gives `c² = b * a⁻¹`, which is exactly why the\nclassical Jones normalising factor carries a square root. Their solvability is a hypothesis here;\nthe descent is the theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.normFactor_stabInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.normFactor_stabInv","kind":"theorem","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L323-L335","doc":"The normalising unit under negative stabilisation: one `c⁻¹` and one extra `d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.normFactor_stab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.normFactor_stab","kind":"theorem","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L312-L321","doc":"The normalising unit under positive stabilisation: one extra `c` (writhe up by one) and one\nextra `d` (level up by one). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.normalise_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.normalise_apply","kind":"theorem","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L307-L310","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.normalise","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.normalise","kind":"def","line":303,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L303-L305","doc":"**The Jones-normalised functional** `c^{writhe} · d^{level} · f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.normFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.normFactor","kind":"def","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L299-L301","doc":"The normalising unit `c^{writhe} · d^{level}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsScaledMarkov.stabInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsScaledMarkov.stabInv","kind":"theorem","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L297-L297","doc":"Negative stabilisation multiplies by `b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsScaledMarkov.stab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsScaledMarkov.stab","kind":"theorem","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L295-L295","doc":"Positive stabilisation multiplies by `a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsScaledMarkov.conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsScaledMarkov.conj","kind":"theorem","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L293-L293","doc":"Invariance under Markov move I. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsScaledMarkov.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsScaledMarkov.mk","kind":"ctor","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L291-L291","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsScaledMarkov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsScaledMarkov","kind":"structure","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L288-L297","doc":"**A scaled Markov functional**: invariant under move I, but multiplied by `a` (resp. `b`) under\npositive (resp. negative) stabilisation. This is the shape of every Markov trace: `a` and `b` are\nthe two Markov parameters `z` and `z'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.Framing.w_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.Framing.w_gen","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L284-L284","doc":"The new generator has writhe one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.Framing.w_incl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.Framing.w_incl","kind":"theorem","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L282-L282","doc":"Stabilisation does not change the writhe of an old braid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.Framing.w","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.Framing.w","kind":"def","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L280-L280","doc":"The writhe homomorphism at each level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.Framing.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.Framing.mk","kind":"ctor","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L278-L278","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.Framing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.Framing","kind":"structure","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L267-L284","doc":"**A framing** on a tower: an exponent-sum (writhe) homomorphism to `Multiplicative ℤ`,\ncompatible with stabilisation and sending the new generator to `1`.\n\n**A framing is supplied as data; none is constructed here for the Artin groups.** The `w` field is\nthe writhe, which for the Artin presentation is `QOU.MathlibExt.Braid.exponentSum` (a different\nfile, not importable here under the Mathlib-only constraint). The other two fields are *not*\navailable for that tower even in principle at present: `w_incl` and `w_gen` are compatibilities\nwith `BraidTower.incl` and `BraidTower.gen`. A tower on the Artin groups exists downstream\n(`QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkovClass.artinTower`), but no `Framing` on it is constructed; the writhe\ncorrection there is carried by `QOU.IwahoriHecke.JonesNormalisation.jonesFn` directly. The only\ntower and framing exhibited in this file are the abelianised ones below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.classOf_eq_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.classOf_eq_iff","kind":"theorem","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L255-L259","doc":"**The quotient is exactly the quotient by `MarkovEquiv`** — two braids have the same class iff\nthey are Markov equivalent. Without this, `MarkovClass` could a priori be coarser than the\nequivalence relation it is meant to realise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsMarkovInvariant.lift_classOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsMarkovInvariant.lift_classOf","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L251-L253","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsMarkovInvariant.lift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsMarkovInvariant.lift","kind":"def","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L246-L249","doc":"**Descent, packaged**: a Markov invariant is a function on Markov classes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.classOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.classOf","kind":"def","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L243-L244","doc":"The class of a braid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.MarkovClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.MarkovClass","kind":"def","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L239-L241","doc":"The set of Markov classes, as the quotient of the tower by the one-step move relation. By\n`classOf_eq_iff` below this really is the quotient by `MarkovEquiv`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsMarkovInvariant.descends","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsMarkovInvariant.descends","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L223-L237","doc":"**THE DESCENT THEOREM.** A functional respecting both Markov moves takes equal values on\nMarkov-equivalent elements of the tower. This is the algebraic half of \"a Markov-invariant of braids\nis an invariant of links\"; the other half (that the classes *are* links) is Markov's topological\ntheorem and is not proved here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsMarkovInvariant.stabInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsMarkovInvariant.stabInv","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L221-L221","doc":"Invariance under negative stabilisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsMarkovInvariant.stab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsMarkovInvariant.stab","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L219-L219","doc":"Invariance under positive stabilisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsMarkovInvariant.conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsMarkovInvariant.conj","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L217-L217","doc":"Invariance under Markov move I. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsMarkovInvariant.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsMarkovInvariant.mk","kind":"ctor","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L215-L215","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsMarkovInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.IsMarkovInvariant","kind":"structure","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L212-L221","doc":"**A Markov invariant**: a functional on the tower that is unchanged by both moves. The three\nfields are the moves themselves, written as equations — no field is `True`, and each is a genuine\nconstraint (violated, for instance, by the writhe alone, which changes under stabilisation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.markovEquiv_stab_stabInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.markovEquiv_stab_stabInv","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L204-L208","doc":"Destabilising once and restabilising with the opposite sign: `incl x * gen n` and\n`incl x * (gen n)⁻¹` are Markov equivalent. A two-move consequence, not an axiom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.markovEquiv_stabInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.markovEquiv_stabInv","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L199-L202","doc":"**Markov move II (negative)**, as an equivalence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.markovEquiv_stab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.markovEquiv_stab","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L194-L197","doc":"**Markov move II (positive)**, as an equivalence. Note both sides live at *different* levels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.markovEquiv_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.markovEquiv_conj","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L187-L192","doc":"**Markov move I in conjugation form**: `u * x * u⁻¹ ~ x`. This is the form the move is usually\nstated in, and it is *derived* from the `a * b ~ b * a` form by taking `a = u * x`, `b = u⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.markovEquiv_mul_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.markovEquiv_mul_comm","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L182-L185","doc":"**Markov move I**, as an equivalence: `a * b ~ b * a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.MarkovEquiv.of_move","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.MarkovEquiv.of_move","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L178-L180","doc":"A single move is a Markov equivalence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.MarkovEquiv.trans","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.MarkovEquiv.trans","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L174-L176","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.MarkovEquiv.symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.MarkovEquiv.symm","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L170-L172","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.MarkovEquiv.refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.MarkovEquiv.refl","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L166-L168","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.markovEquiv_equivalence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.markovEquiv_equivalence","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L162-L164","doc":"Markov equivalence **is** an equivalence relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.MarkovEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.MarkovEquiv","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L156-L158","doc":"**Markov equivalence**: the equivalence relation generated by the two moves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.Move.stabInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.Move.stabInv","kind":"ctor","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L154-L154","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.Move.stab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.Move.stab","kind":"ctor","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L153-L153","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.Move.conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.Move.conj","kind":"ctor","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L152-L152","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.Move","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.Move","kind":"inductive","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L143-L154","doc":"**The Markov moves, as a one-step relation.**\n\n* `conj` — Markov move I: `a * b ~ b * a` at a fixed level.\n* `stab` — Markov move II (positive): `x ~ incl x * gen n`, raising the level by one.\n* `stabInv` — Markov move II (negative), with `(gen n)⁻¹`.\n\nThe relation is deliberately *not* symmetric or reflexive; `MarkovEquiv` is its equivalence\nclosure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.Tot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.Tot","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L137-L139","doc":"An element of the tower: a level together with a braid at that level. Stabilisation moves\nbetween levels, so the moves live on this sigma type and not on any fixed `B n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.BraidTower.gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.BraidTower.gen","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L135-L135","doc":"The new generator at level `n+1` (classically `σₙ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.BraidTower.incl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.BraidTower.incl","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L133-L133","doc":"The stabilisation homomorphism `B n → B (n+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.BraidTower.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.BraidTower.mk","kind":"ctor","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L131-L131","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.BraidTower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovMoves.BraidTower","kind":"structure","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovMoves.lean#L127-L135","doc":"**A braid-like tower.** A family of groups `B 0, B 1, …` together with a stabilisation\nhomomorphism `incl n : B n →* B (n+1)` and the new generator `gen n : B (n+1)` that stabilisation\nmakes available. For the Artin braid groups, `incl` is the \"add an unbraided strand\" inclusion and\n`gen n = σₙ`; nothing below depends on that reading. ","signatureChunk":0}]}